WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.940
Infinity War may feel like the climax to the
Marvel film universe, but it's only going

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:05.940
mark a new beginning.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.680
There are a slew of Marvel flicks scheduled
to hit cinemas over the next few years.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.620
As franchises continue to grow and expand
their rosters, it's getting harder to keep

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.940
track of everything that's happening.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.880
Here's every movie Marvel has planned after
Infinity War, both within the MCU and across

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.900
other franchises.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.860
Ant-Man and the Wasp

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.340
Marvel released the first Ant-Man and the
Wasp trailer a little earlier than expected,

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.600
dropping it the day after the Black Panther
premiere.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.440
Director Peyton Reed announced that the film
had wrapped in November 2017, but because

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.910
of it comes out after Infinity War, fans assumed
that details would be scarce until after Thanos

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.840
shows up on Earth.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.710
Judging from the trailer, however, it appears
that Ant-Man and the Wasp will take place

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.740
before the events of Infinity War.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.600
The trailer opens with hero Scott Lang discussing
the aftermath of Civil War with partner-in-crime-stopping

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.230
Hope van Dyne, and there's no sign that Earth's
been shattered by Thanos and his Black Order.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:59.239
Instead, the plot looks like it will center
around Lang going on the run with Hank Pym,

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.940
whose shrinking technology is now in high
demand by all manner of shady types.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.280
The trailer also gives us our first glimpse
at Laurence Fishburne as Dr. Bill Foster,

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:11.250
a scientist who became known as Black Goliath
in Marvel comics after messing with the Pym

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.800
Particle and gaining powers.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.840
There was no sign of Michelle Pfeiffer, however,
who will be appearing as Hank Pym's wife.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.100
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige told
fans that Pfeiffer was their "dream choice"

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.140
in the role of Janet van Dyne, the first owner
of the Wasp suit.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:25.740
Captain Marvel

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.439
We've known for some time now that Brie Larson
will be Captain Marvel, but what we've all

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.940
been dying to find out is whether or not she'll
be showing up in Infinity War.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.960
Turns out she definitely won't be.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.980
Co-director Joe Russo put an end to the rumor
while speaking to ComicBook.com.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.180
Of course, the fact that Russo specifically
denied her involvement in the third Avengers

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.570
flick seems to indicate that she will indeed
appear in Avengers 4, which will hit screens

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.140
after Captain Marvel in 2019.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.640
As far as the rest of the casting is concerned,
Jude Law and Ben Mendelsohn have both agreed

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.940
to terms and will appearing as Mar-Vell and
Yon-Rogg, according to MovieWeb.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.560
Lee Pace has also signed on to reprise his
role as Ronan the Accuser, despite having

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.360
exploded in Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.690
Captain Marvel enthusiasts still shouldn't
expect a rigidly faithful adaptation of the

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.440
source material.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.320
Untitled Avengers: Infinity War sequel

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.390
Marvel originally wanted to shoot Avengers
3 and 4 together, though in the end that approach

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.760
proved too big an ask for the studio, given
the sheer size of the ensemble cast, many

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.460
of whom are in high demand elsewhere.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:30.000
Chris Pratt, for example, has had to juggle
Marvel duties with the Jurassic World sequel.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:33.770
The problem looks like it might get worse
going forward, as the Russos have revealed

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:38.840
that they're considering as many as 67 named
characters for inclusion in Infinity War.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.580
Even Pepper Potts is rumored to be suiting
up for the big showdown with Thanos.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.900
"Are you in The Avengers?

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:44.660
The next Avengers?"

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.040
"I... am I allowed to say?"

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.120
"I say you are!"

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.340
"Okay, I am, I am!"

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.400
The title of the sequel is being kept under
wraps at Marvel, because it's a spoiler for

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.060
Infinity War.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.400
Joe Russo explained:

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.240
"It is certainly part of the concept of the
title is that it's advancing the narrative.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.980
We're gonna sit on that until we feel the
time is right and when people have absorbed

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.060
the first movie enough."

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.640
Untitled Spider-Man: Homecoming sequel

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.340
After Marvel and Sony finally came to a mutually
beneficial arrangement regarding the use of

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.660
Spider-Man, it seemed unlikely that the wall
crawler would get just a single solo movie

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.280
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.350
Tom Holland made his debut as Peter Parker
in 2016's Captain America: Civil War before

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.720
fronting his own standalone movie last summer,
and he confirmed that a sequel was in the

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.720
pipeline, saying:

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.430
"We've just finished Spider-Man [Homecoming]
and we're talking about the second one and

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.560
who the villain is going to be and where we're
going."

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.600
According to recent reports, Parker will be
facing off against a female enemy this time

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.100
out.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.680
Marvel is apparently on the hunt for a European
actress in her 20s to play a "femme fatale"

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:47.020
type, and emerging details on principal photography
are leading many to assume that some of the

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:51.540
movie will be set in Europe, with a tentative
release date of July 2019.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.040
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.860
If Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 3 was ever
in doubt at Marvel Studios, the box office

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.720
numbers posted by the second film have made
certain that the team will be back for a third

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.220
round.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.320
But Star-Lord might not be taking center stage
this time out.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:10.690
James Gunn told USA Today that he's already
begun working on the screenplay for the third

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.770
film, which will apparently involve less Chris
Pratt and more Zoe Saldana — the director

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.840
said he's talked with the actress about having
Gamora take a more prominent role in the final

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:19.760
Guardians outing.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.660
Casting news is already starting to trickle
through, with Gunn confirming that Elizabeth

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:28.100
Debicki will reprise her role as Ayesha, the
Golden High Priestess of the Sovereign.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:32.139
There's nothing official in terms of release
date yet, although Gunn has hinted that we'll

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.320
be seeing Volume 3 sometime in 2020.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.100
Ant-Man 3

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:42.060
Marvel Studios is clearly expecting the upcoming
Ant-Man sequel to go down well: A third installment

00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:45.919
in the Paul Rudd-led franchise is already
in the pipeline, according to co-star Michael

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:46.420
Peña.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:51.300
Speaking to IGN about his film 12 Strong,
Pena let slip that Ant-Man 3 is happening,

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.740
although he wasn't sure if he'd be needed
for it, saying:

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.139
"It's a whole different kind of club to be
in, the Marvel Universe.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.780
I don't know if they'll use me for the third
movie, I still really don't know.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.479
It's cool to make a little bit of a mark on
that Marvel Universe and it's kind of a cool

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.040
club, they run a really cool studio."

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:06.880
Black Widow

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.800
Scarlett Johansson made her debut as former
KGB spy Natasha Romanoff, aka Black Widow,

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.640
in 2010's Iron Man 2.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:18.780
"I want one."

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:19.500
"No."

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.780
Eight years later, we're still waiting for
official confirmation of her solo movie.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:28.880
Kevin Feige first hinted at a Black Widow
standalone feature in 2014 when he said that

00:05:28.889 --> 00:05:31.230
her part in the MCU was "very big" and that

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.979
"The notion of exploring that even further
in her own film would be great."

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.400
He reiterated that Marvel was committed to
making the film happen in 2016, saying:

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.400
"I would say certainly the one, creatively
and emotionally, that we are most committing

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.680
to doing is Black Widow."

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:49.260
Another two years went without much news,
though a recent Variety exclusive claims that

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:53.180
the wheels are finally in motion on Black
Widow and that Marvel has hired Jac Schaeffer

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.080
to pen the script.

00:05:54.409 --> 00:05:58.300
Johansson was consulted over the decision
to enlist Schaeffer, though Variety's sources

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.509
say the movie is still in early development
and doesn't have any plot details so far.

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:03.659
We do have one suggestion:

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.840
"The only thing missing in Black Widow's life…"

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:07.360
"Oops.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.880
Such a klutz."
"...was love."

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:10.600
"Hey.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.780
I'm Ultron."

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.560
Doctor Doom

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:19.930
The Fantastic Four don't have a particularly
great track record in movies, but a surprise

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:24.420
announcement at San Diego Comic Con 2017 gave
some new hope to fans.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:29.190
Noah Hawley, the creator of the FX series
Legion, wrapped up his show's panel by revealing

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:33.529
that he was working with Fox to develop a
movie for the Fantastic Four's most iconic

00:06:33.529 --> 00:06:35.500
villain, teasing it with two words:

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.600
"The first one is 'Doctor' and the second
one is 'Doom.'"

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.910
Since then, Fox has been bought out by Disney,
leaving question marks over some properties

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:45.560
in the early stages of development.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:49.800
Hawley insists that the movie is still happening,
although even he's not sure when, telling

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:50.460
Collider:

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:54.360
"On some level, we're still looking at a period
of time — probably a year, at the least

00:06:54.369 --> 00:06:56.059
— for this whole thing to go through.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.930
[…] I've been waiting for the phone to ring
to see if anyone is gonna have an opinion."

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.680
"Doom needs no one."

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.540
Silver and Black

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.479
There's a lot of focus on Tom Hardy's Venom
at the moment, but Sony has also set the wheels

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.560
in motion on Silver and Black, another upcoming
feature based on the studio's Spider-Man portfolio.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.960
Silver Sable has been both an ally and an
enemy to Spider-Man over the years, but has

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:20.080
never been portrayed on the big screen before.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.520
Black Cat on the other hand, did pop up in
The Amazing Spider-Man 2.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:28.810
Well, kind of: Rogue One star Felicity Jones
briefly appeared as a character called Felicia

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.780
Hardy, Black Cat's real name in the comics.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:34.819
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Chris
Yost, who worked on Thor: Ragnarok, has been

00:07:34.819 --> 00:07:39.810
hired to tidy up a script penned by Lisa Joy,
the co-creator of HBO's critically acclaimed

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:40.310
Westworld.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:44.520
Gina Prince-Bythewood is slated to direct,
although the latest rumors suggest the film

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.320
was recently put on indefinite hold.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.320
"Some things never change."

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:51.340
Laura

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:56.740
Daphne Keen definitely impressed as Wolverine's
offspring Laura in Logan, and director James

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.990
Mangold revealed that the success of Wonder
Woman has brought a solo outing for the character

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:01.980
closer to reality.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:02.980
He said:

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:07.589
"That film only solidifies more for studios
that there's less to fear with a female protagonist.

00:08:07.589 --> 00:08:11.499
The more that keeps getting hit home, that
ends up giving me more space turning around

00:08:11.499 --> 00:08:14.210
and going, 'Well, here we are with a female
protagonist.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:15.210
That's incredible.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.750
And what are we going to do with her?'

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.980
And that's where we are with that right now,
dreaming."

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.080
X-Men: Dark Phoenix

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:26.840
This direct follow-up to 2016's X-Men: Apocalypse
will bring back all the big-hitters from the

00:08:26.849 --> 00:08:31.080
previous movie, with the addition of Jessica
Chastain as one of the film's villains.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:35.360
Dark Phoenix will mark the directorial debut
of Simon Kinberg, although Kinberg has been

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.510
working on the X-Men films as a writer and
producer since 2006's The Last Stand, a botched

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:43.070
attempt at adapting the classic Dark Phoenix
Saga.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:47.150
Kinberg confirmed that the film will follow
the franchise's decade-skipping trend, jumping

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.260
forward from the '80s-set Apocalypse to a
'90s setting.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:53.120
It's scheduled to open November 2018.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:54.700
Multiple Man

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:59.580
After directing Dark Phoenix, Simon Kinberg
will return to the producer's chair to oversee

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:02.340
yet another spinoff in Fox's X-Men franchise.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:06.460
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Kinberg
is in negotiations with James Franco over

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:10.930
the lead role in a planned adaptation of Multiple
Man, a mutant with the power to create and

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.360
control clones of himself.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:15.700
"Cripes."

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:20.700
While casual viewers probably won't recall
the name James Madrox, the character has actually

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.120
popped up in Fox's X-Men movies before.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:28.080
He was portrayed by Eric Dane in 2006's X-Men:
The Last Stand, appearing as one of the mutants

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.340
recruited by Magneto.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.020
Gambit

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:37.000
In development since 2014, Gambit seemed like
a sure thing when an X-Men producer confirmed

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.460
that Channing Tatum would play the card-tossing
mutant.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:43.660
After several directors left the film, Gore
Verbinski jumped into the hot seat and was

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:48.650
eyeing a Valentine's Day 2019 release, although
The Hollywood Reporter later confirmed that

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:52.660
Verbinski has become the third director to
walk, leaving the seemingly cursed project

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:53.740
in limbo once more.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.600
Fox has reacted by pushing the release date
to summer 2019, giving itself some breathing

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.800
room just in case they can't find a replacement.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.680
Tatum remains attached, along with Lizzy Caplan,
who has been cast as the film's female lead.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.620
Hopefully, Tatum keeps Gambit's Cajun accent.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.760
"Pop go dah weasel."

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.060
Venom

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:19.000
Sony had been discussing a Venom movie for
over a decade when the studio finally confirmed

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.380
that the symbiote's solo adventure was going
ahead.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:25.280
Tom Hardy is playing Eddie Brock, the first
character to take on the Venom moniker in

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.240
Marvel comics.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:30.580
Despite being a fan favorite, the anti-hero
has only been portrayed in film once, when

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:33.000
Topher Grace donned the black for Spider-Man
3.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.160
"Oh yeah, I know all about you."

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:41.740
Hardy is set to play a central role in what's
being dubbed the Sony Marvel Universe, and

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.720
director Ruben Fleischer revealed that the
film would follow the Planet of the Symbiotes

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.620
and Lethal Protector comic arcs.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.600
Venom is slated for an October 2017 release.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.040
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:58.130
African-Latino Spider-Man Miles Morales was
only supposed to be around for four years

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.380
in the pages of Marvel's comics as part of
the Ultimate Marvel imprint.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.980
But this version of Spidey proved so popular
that Marvel decided to merge him into the

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:10.070
main line, and now he'll be the focus of a
feature-length animated movie.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:14.200
At present, the film is scheduled to be released
on December 21st, 2018.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:15.920
New Mutants

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.980
Marvel fans everywhere got a thrill from the
trailer for New Mutants.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.221
The horror-inspired X-Men spinoff is being
helmed by young filmmaker Josh Boone, who

00:11:24.221 --> 00:11:28.510
took it upon himself personally to convince
Fox it was a property worth adapting.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:32.360
He and co-writer Knate Gwaltney put together
their own New Mutants comic book based on

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:35.540
stories they wanted to adapt for Fox, and
the studio loved it.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.640
Boone explained:

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:40.080
"It walked them through a trilogy of New Mutant
films that would build on each other.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.690
[It] took all the images we had loved from
the series and strung them together to show

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:45.380
them the movie we wanted to do."

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.040
Even then, it took a long time for the film
to happen.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.580
"We spent a couple years writing the script
before I went and shot the movie.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.520
[...] We worked on it for two or three years,
I think."

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:57.380
Shooting has already wrapped on the film,
and fans can expect to see it in theaters

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.060
in August 2019.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:00.860
Deadpool 2

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:07.100
After 2016's Deadpool unexpectedly became
the highest-grossing film in the X-Men franchise,

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.000
keeping the creative team together for the
follow-up seemed essential.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:14.080
That wasn't to be the case — director Tim
Miller soon departed the project, and David

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.440
Leitch of John Wick fame has since stepped
up to direct.

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:20.420
Josh Brolin will also be welcomed into the
fold as the time-traveler Cable.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:25.740
Fox dedicated an entire trailer to introducing
the character, emphasizing his war-torn past.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:31.000
The trailers also confirmed that Brianna Hildebrand
would be returning as Negasonic Teenage Warhead

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:35.440
and that T.J. Miller would reprise his role
as Weasel, along with a whole new cast of

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:35.940
mutants.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.680
Deadpool 2 arrives on May 18th.

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:39.320
X-Force

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.840
Another project promised by Fox is X-Force,
a black ops team of Marvel mutants far more

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.170
brutal than the X-Men.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.240
The film will revolve around Deadpool and
Cable.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.800
"X-Force!"

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:51.260
"Isn't that a little derivative?"

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:52.780
"You're absolutely right."

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:58.410
A report picked up by MovieWeb states that
X-Force will begin filming in October 2018,

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.960
with Drew Goddard attached to direct.

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:05.240
According to a recent Discussing Film exclusive,
the green light remains firmly on for Goddard's

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.420
X-Force, regardless of the Disney takeover.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:08.720
Thanks for watching!

